    "details": {
      "isComplex": true,
      "level": {
        "value": 5
      },
      "disable": "<p>@Check[type:diplomacy|dc:26|name:To Convince Haunt Of All the Grand Accomplishments They've Completed|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) To Convince Haunt Of All the Grand Accomplishments They've Completed,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:occultism|dc:23|name:To Banish Spirit|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) To Banish Spirit,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:religion|dc:23|name: To Banish Spirit|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) To Banish Spirit,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:perception|dc:20|name:To Hear Book Pages Rustling|traits:complex,haunt] To Hear Book Pages Rustling.</p>",
      "description": "<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> When the PC haunted by insanity enters this room, dozens of memories of expeditions, sea voyages, and travels to exotic locales race through his mind, remnants of Traver Foxglove’s journeys before he settled down here in Varisia. As the memories build momentum, they become increasingly infused with a sense of bitter disappointment and regret, and the character becomes increasingly aware that he is now receiving memories that never were, memories of fantastic discoveries he could have made had he not chosen to settle down with a shrill harpy of a wife.</p>",
      "reset": "<p>The haunt automatically resets after 1 day until the supernatural fungus in B37 is dealt with, even if the haunt was previously disabled.</p>",
      "routine": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Insane Haunt: </strong>This haunt affects those haunted by Traveler Foxglove after being slowiy driven to madness. This haunt affects impulsive or untrustworthy characters. lf no creature in a group ﬁts this description it may effect any creature in a group</p>"
    },
